# Port Meridian

An original open-world crime game that plays offline in a desktop browser.
You are **Rex Marlowe**, a courier who owes **$4,000** to **Marisol Vega**,
the fixer who runs Vega Motors. Do her five missions to clear the debt —
or keep the money and walk away.

Everything in the game is original: the city, the characters, the vehicles,
the names, the story, the art and the sound. No real city, person, brand or
franchise appears in it.

## Play it

```sh
node serve.ts
# then open http://localhost:8080
```

Or open `game/index.html` straight from a static file server. No build
step, no library, no network request — plain HTML, CSS and ES modules.

## The city

**Port Meridian** is a dense 1.5 km city on a 9×9 road grid with four
districts, each with its own look:

- **Old Town** (north-west) — terracotta rooftops and narrow streets
- **Downtown** (north-east) — glass towers, the bank, the Meridian Hotel
- **The Shores** (south-west) — pastel houses and the park
- **Portside** (south-east) — warehouses, docks and the harbor

Eight landmarks anchor it: Vega Motors, Rex's Apartment (the safehouse),
the Port Warehouse, Meridian City Bank, PMPD Headquarters, General
Hospital, the Meridian Hotel and Meridian Park. A day/night cycle runs
over the whole city — dusk falls around 18:30, headlights come on at
night.

## Systems

- **On foot and by car** — walk, sprint, aim with the mouse, or drive any
  car you can reach. Seven car models with different speed, grip and
  toughness, from the Comet Sedan to the Falcon GT.
- **Traffic and pedestrians** — traffic cars follow the road graph, stop
  at red lights and keep their distance; pedestrians walk the sidewalks,
  cross at intersections and flee gunfire.
- **Stealing cars** — take a parked car freely, or pull the driver out of
  a moving one and earn a wanted star for it.
- **Wanted system and police** — 0–5 stars. The PMPD chases in cars,
  hunts on foot, shoots back at 3+ stars and sets roadblocks at 5 stars.
  Break line of sight and the heat cools, one star at a time.
- **Missions and story** — five missions with story cards: a timed
  delivery, a repo job from a guarded lot, tailing a courier van without
  being spotted, a three-star getaway, and a shootout at the warehouse
  that ends in a choice about the money.
- **Combat** — fists, pistol and SMG, with reloads, spread, muzzle flash
  and bullets that buildings and cars stop.
- **Side work** — drive a taxi for fares, and find the 10 hidden cash
  packages scattered around the city.
- **HUD with a live minimap** — wanted stars, cash, respect, health,
  ammo, speed, district, clock, objective marker and an off-screen arrow.
- **Title screen and save** — New Game / Continue, a save slot, and
  autosave after every mission (localStorage).

## Controls

| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| W A S D / arrows | Move on foot, drive |
| Mouse | Aim (on foot) |
| Click | Shoot |
| E | Enter / exit car, start mission |
| Q / 1–3 | Switch weapon |
| R | Reload |
| Space | Handbrake |
| Shift | Sprint |
| P / Esc | Pause |
| M | Mute |

## How it is built

- `game/index.html` — the page, one canvas
- `game/src/config.js` — tuning, palettes, districts, car models, weapons
- `game/src/random.js` — seeded RNG (mulberry32) and math helpers
- `game/src/city.js` — road graph, blocks, buildings, traffic lights
- `game/src/vehicles.js` — car physics and traffic AI
- `game/src/pedestrians.js` — pedestrian AI
- `game/src/police.js` — wanted system, pursuit, roadblocks
- `game/src/player.js` — the player, on foot and driving, weapons
- `game/src/combat.js` — bullets, enemies, particles, skid marks
- `game/src/missions.js` — the five-mission story arc
- `game/src/world.js` — all systems in one DOM-free world
- `game/src/render.js` — canvas drawing, HUD, minimap, screens
- `game/src/input.js` — keyboard and mouse
- `game/src/audio.js` — procedural WebAudio music and effects
- `game/src/save.js` — localStorage save
- `game/src/shots.js` — the four staged screenshots
- `game/src/main.js` — boot, fixed-timestep loop, screens
- `main.ts` — the make.fun hand-in (copies `game/` + `screenshots/` to
  `/output` and writes `dossier.json`)

The four screenshots in `screenshots/` are staged through the game's own
systems (`?shot=chase|steal|mission|title`): a dusk chase at 3 stars, a
car theft in progress, mission 3 with its story card, and the title
screen with a save slot.

